{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And I, the he-goat</b> — this is Alexander of Macedon, and so the angel interpreted. And he comes from the west, for he was king of the Arabs [?] and there he was born. And the meaning of <b>and none touched the ground</b>: as though he flew in the air in his running, and from the abundance of his running it did not appear that he touched the ground." "<b>And the he-goat</b> — <i>se'ir izim</i> (a he-goat). Thus it is written <b>וצפירי עזים</b>, in the book of Ezra." "<b>A notable horn</b> — it is obscure [מסובך], and so the angel interpreted it, that it is the first king who killed Artaxerxes. It is in the Aramaean tongue [לשון כשדים]. And I will explain further."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The text reads מלך הערב ('king of the Arabs'); Alexander was not king of the Arabs nor born in Arabia. Possibly a textual error, translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:26.454969109Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}